  "verdict": "partly",
  "why": "One seed with one q leaves nothing at lag 1 for 7 of 10 walkers. It fails to whiten every one of the four hearts. Old Faithful leans against its last wait, so the best-fitting slope on the seed is -0.584: an averaging seed with positive weights does not make that. All three of the lens's written predictions held. The walking result is not strong: a record with nothing left to whiten passes the same band only about two times in three, and under a flat band of 0.03 fewer walkers pass. None of this is evidence for CRR; it sorts three systems by how far back their gaps reach, with ordinary tools.",
